    <!-- Recording permission explanation -->
    <string name="record_permissions_title">About in-app recording</string>
    <string name="record_permissions_body">Built-in recording uses CameraX and needs the Camera permission (to see you) and Microphone permission (to record audio); if you deny the microphone, video is still recorded silently. On Android 13+ the Notification permission only controls the "recording in progress" notification. If you deny Camera, use \u201COpen camera app\u201D instead \u2014 that is the external workflow, where the teleprompter floats over your own camera app and no in-app permissions are needed.</string>
